original results from the statistical analysis of experimental    9437 1451     
data by P.G. Young using the GLUCS code. The modification         9437 1451     
introduced in the fast energy range for the average prompt neutron9437 1451     
multiplicity in the ENDF/B-VII library is removed. The average    9437 1451     
total neutron multiplicity is adjusted accordingly.               9437 1451     
                                                                  9437 1451     
*** MF3, MT18                                                     9437 1451     
                                                                  9437 1451     
The fission cross section evaluated as part of the 2016 standard  9437 1451     
evaluation is adopted here above 40 keV and up to 20 MeV.         9437 1451     
                                                                  9437 1451     
*** MF3, MT102                                                    9437 1451     
                                                                  9437 1451     
The capture cross section follows the recent modification of      9437 1451     
ENDF/B-VII.1 above 30 keV to better match recent DANCE data by    9437 1451     
Mosby et al. [Mo16] up to 0.7 MeV, where it switches to Kawano's  9437 1451     
CoH3 calculations [Ka16] up to 3.7 MeV. For now (to be replaced), 9437 1451     
from 3.7 to 20 MeV, it then matches the previous ENDF/B-VII.1     9437 1451     
evaluation.                                                       9437 1451     
                                                                  9437 1451     
*** MF5, MT18                                                     9437 1451     
                                                                  9437 1451     
The PFNS was obtained from an evaluation by Neudecker et al.[Ne16]9437 1451     
extending the original Los Alamos model to include the effects of 9437 1451     
emission anisotropy and different fragment temperatures, as well  9437 1451     
as to properly account for multi-chance fission evaporation and   9437 1451     
pre-equilibrium neutron spectra. The thermal PFNS was obtained by 9437 1451     
averaging the ENDF/B-VII.1 PFNS with a slightly modified PFNS by  9437 1451     
Romano.                                                           9437 1451     
                                                                  9437 1451     
[Mo16] S. Mosby et al, private communication, publication for     9437 1451     
Phys. Rev. C in preparation.                                      9437 1451     
                                                                  9437 1451     
[Ka16] T. Kawano, private communication.                          9437 1451     
                                                                  9437 1451     
[Ne16] D. Neudecker, P. Talou, T. Kawano, A.C. Kahler, M.E. Rising9437 1451     
 and M.C. White, EPJ Web of Conferences 111, 05004 (2016).        9437 1451     
